>
>    I've compiled the X11 nethack, but I've been unable to get the individual
>characters to appear in different colors the way PC nethack does, i.e., the
>little dog `d' is not white.  I've #def'ed TEXTCOLOR, but that doesn't
>seem to work.

I got it to work on the local machines by putting 'color' in the
nethack options (either in your .nethackrc or in the NETHACKOPTIONS env
variable).  Try that; if it doesn't work, well, then I don't know :-).

Also, you may want to redefine some of the colors if you do
get it working; I redefined 'gray' as 'white' and 'black' as 'gray',
so that I could see them.  (You do this in your .Xdefaults; mail me
if you wanna know how :-)
